# Mac Finder metadata. The formerly-tracked .DS_Store and man/.DS_Store were
# untracked via `git rm --cached` (S488) -- a .gitignore rule alone has no effect
# on already-tracked files, which is why they kept reappearing in `git status`.
.DS_Store

# User's local-only copyrighted reference material (full-text journal articles/pages under
# publisher copyright, no open-access marking) -- kept off this PUBLIC repo deliberately.
# Session 479 (2026-08-08), see CHANGELOG.md and PROJECT_LEARNINGS.md Learning 479. This does
# NOT cover inst/extdata/reference/Master_Genetic_metrics_2_14_15.pdf, an unpublished NPRC
# working-group document already committed (S418) -- a different copyright situation.
inst/extdata/reference/5201430.pdf
inst/extdata/reference/bioinformatics_24_2_279.pdf
inst/extdata/reference/pedigree_nomenclature.html

# kinship2's own supplementary material (Sinnwell/Therneau/Schaid, Mayo Clinic) -- an NIHMS
# (NIH Manuscript Submission) PMC deposit, so unlike the 3 files directly above it DOES carry
# NIH public-access marking (free reading access via PMC). That is not the same as a
# redistribution/repackaging license: PMC deposit terms guarantee public reading access, not
# third-party bundling rights the original publisher (historically a subscription journal) may
# still hold. Kept off this PUBLIC repo out of the same caution as the 3 files above, pending a
# confirmed license check -- not because it fails the "no open-access marking" test those 3
# were excluded under. Session 567 (2026-08-14), owner decision via AskUserQuestion, see
# CHANGELOG.md.
inst/extdata/reference/NIHMS593658-supplement-supplement_1.pdf

# 3 personal reference files ("The Compounding Loop") saved from a Claude Artifact about this
# project's own SESSION_RUNNER.md/SAFEGUARDS.md methodology (github.com/KJ5HST/methodology) --
# not scientific/genetics reference material like the files above, and unrelated to this
# package's own subject matter. Kept off this PUBLIC repo as personal reference, matching the
# same "gitignore in place" pattern established for the files above. A 4th file found alongside
# these 3, a Microsoft/LibreOffice editor lock file with no content
# ("~$e Compounding Loop.html"), was deleted outright rather than gitignored. Session 568,
# 2026-08-14, owner decision via AskUserQuestion, see CHANGELOG.md.
inst/extdata/reference/The Compounding Loop.html
inst/extdata/reference/The Compounding Loop.pdf
inst/extdata/reference/The Compounding Loop.webarchive

# Python bytecode cache from methodology_dashboard.py/methodology_trim.py (Session 514)
__pycache__/
